### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Order API — OPEN SESSION (POST /api/v1/sessions)
#
# How to run: VS Code REST Client — click "Send Request" top to bottom.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - Docker stack up with the Order module: docker compose up -d --build
#   - Seeded chain admin exists: admin@devtunde.com / Password123!
#
# Contract (ticket 0016):
#   - Only CASHIER + MANAGER operate the till (title gate, Q1).
#   - One non-CLOSED session per operator, chain-wide (Q9).
#   - The session inherits the operator's employing store.
#
# `# Expected:` labels the status each request proves.
# Tokens expire after 15 MINUTES — re-send the setup from the top.
# Captures are session-scoped: a "No value is resolved" error means
# re-send the setup requests from the top of this file.
# All data is FAKE (devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### 1 — Setup: chain admin logs in
# @name adminLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: mint the store's seat admin (fresh persona per run)
# @name seatSignup
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Order Seat Admin",
  "email": "ord-seat-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567"
}

### 3 — Setup: seat admin logs in
# @name seatLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{seatSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4 — Setup: chain admin creates the store, seating that admin
# @name store
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "brand": "Order Probe Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "KIOSK",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{seatLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Probe Way",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "ord-store-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 5 — Setup: seat admin hires a cashier (the password we send IS the password)
# @name hire
# Expected: 201 — no secrets echo in the response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Order Cashier",
  "email": "ord-cashier-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234568",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 6 — Setup: the hired cashier logs in with the password the hire set
# @name cashierLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hire.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 7 — THE HAPPY PATH: the cashier opens a session
# @name session
# Expected: 201 — status ACTIVE, storePublicId = the employing store,
# closedAt absent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8 — The cashier tries to open a SECOND session while the first is open
# Expected: 409 — one non-CLOSED session per operator (Q9)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9 — Setup: hire a SALES_ATTENDANT (the title-gate persona)
# @name hireAttendant
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Order Attendant",
  "email": "ord-attendant-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234569",
  "jobTitle": "SALES_ATTENDANT"
}

### 10 — Setup: the attendant logs in
# @name attendantLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hireAttendant.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 11 — The attendant opens a session — the title gate refuses (Q1)
# Expected: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{attendantLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 12 — Setup: signup a stranger with no employment anywhere
# @name strangerSignup
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Order Stranger",
  "email": "ord-stranger-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234570"
}

### 13 — Setup: the stranger logs in
# @name strangerLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{strangerSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 14 — The stranger opens a session — no employment, no till
# Expected: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{strangerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 15 — Anonymous open — no token at all
# Expected: 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions

### 16 — Close the setup session — the shift envelope seals
# Expected: 200 — status CLOSED, closedAt stamped
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{session.response.body.publicId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 17 — The SAME cashier opens a FRESH session after closing
# Expected: 201 — a CLOSED row releases the one-slot (reopen is legal)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
